00:12:47.616 --> 00:12:48.857
any group sessions.

00:12:49.297 --> 00:12:52.400
They're concerned about reputation.

00:12:53.308 --> 00:12:59.713
No one in my life, on my circle, even
noticed that I was in treatment.

00:13:00.393 --> 00:13:03.156
How much were you spending on your drug
habit and drink habit?

00:13:03.756 --> 00:13:07.999
There was no problem to spend 50,000 in
the night or more.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:13.183
People who live this type of lifestyle,
they also spend a lot of money on inviting

00:13:13.203 --> 00:13:13.903
other people.

00:13:14.284 --> 00:13:18.887
I was really able to party for three days
and go to work like nothing happened.

00:13:19.988 --> 00:13:23.989
Can you describe what your life was like
when you were at your lowest point during

00:13:24.009 --> 00:13:24.709
addiction?

00:13:24.709 --> 00:13:28.470
The last time I chatted, I had from Cannes
to Sardinia.

00:13:29.311 --> 00:13:35.252
I remember that at some point I was
throwing up overboard and people were

00:13:35.292 --> 00:13:36.193
lying there and they

00:13:36.194 --> 00:13:39.794
were all messed up and I didn't even
remember where they came from.

00:13:40.934 --> 00:13:42.534
It was very lonely.

00:13:43.355 --> 00:13:47.716
My life was going too fast to nowhere.

00:13:48.928 --> 00:13:54.432
I looked at the Mediterranean Sea and
there was a beautiful

00:13:55.113 --> 00:13:59.997
sunrise and I felt like you've got to
change something.

00:14:01.138 --> 00:14:03.200
And is that when you came to Paracelsus?

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:03.920
After that, yes.

00:14:04.461 --> 00:14:10.365
So I stayed, I think, for two months and
then I came back and used

00:14:10.646 --> 00:14:13.968
Paracelsus as my support system.

00:14:14.729 --> 00:14:16.310
And how much did you spend in total?

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:18.692
It was like 800, 200 million, yeah.

00:14:19.344 --> 00:14:21.765
Can you give us a rough idea of how
wealthy you are?

00:14:22.385 --> 00:14:23.746
Well, I don't know what I would say.

00:14:24.486 --> 00:14:27.467
It would be enough to stay for the rest of
my life at Paracelsus.

00:14:32.289 --> 00:14:36.251
It's easy to see how Paracelsus could
become a temporary escape for people whose

00:14:36.291 --> 00:14:38.392
lives at the mortuary have no budgetary
limits.

00:14:41.994 --> 00:14:45.115
People of that power, money can keep them
going for a long time.

00:14:45.355 --> 00:14:47.676
So the rock bottom is when they end up in
the emergency room.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:52.407
or sometimes in a morgue.

00:14:52.527 --> 00:14:56.113
It's hard for the average population to
really have empathy for somebody who has

00:14:56.134 --> 00:14:59.259
it all, who can afford everything, to
actually be

00:14:59.319 --> 00:15:00.019
allowed to.

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:01.221
suffer and have problems.

00:15:01.981 --> 00:15:04.443
At some point that kind of lifestyle
becomes a bit dull.

00:15:05.283 --> 00:15:09.726
Boredom is a big factor when you have a
lot of wealth and really no purpose.

00:15:10.226 --> 00:15:13.188
You need a reason to get out of bed in the
morning and that's not just to go to the

00:15:13.189 --> 00:15:13.889
next party.

00:15:13.889 --> 00:15:15.629
That purpose doesn't last very long.

00:15:15.789 --> 00:15:19.892
That really isolates and in the end it's
that loneliness and the pain that comes

00:15:19.912 --> 00:15:22.233
from that loneliness and often also
associated boredom

00:15:22.954 --> 00:15:26.696
that leads to this pain and inner void
that the people start to self-medicate.

00:15:32.464 --> 00:15:37.947
You know, you were seven years old and you
probably were fully aware of the tension

00:15:38.067 --> 00:15:39.168
between your mum and dad.

00:15:39.848 --> 00:15:45.831
And then the anxiety kicks in, just
letting it all go and drugs and crazy and

00:15:45.832 --> 00:15:46.532
that just made it

00:15:46.532 --> 00:15:47.193
worse.

00:15:47.193 --> 00:15:47.953
It never went away.

00:15:49.693 --> 00:15:51.454
Do you know what you're feeling now?

00:15:52.635 --> 00:15:56.377
It's quite intense, isn't it?

00:15:56.378 --> 00:15:57.078
Of course.

00:15:57.078 --> 00:15:58.879
I think we're talking about your dad.

00:16:00.479 --> 00:16:01.420
I think that's what's going on.

00:16:08.435 --> 00:16:11.517
Do you want us to leave?

00:16:11.537 --> 00:16:12.237
Yeah, alright.

00:16:12.237 --> 00:16:12.698
Thanks.

00:16:12.718 --> 00:16:13.418
Thanks.

00:16:13.418 --> 00:16:18.323
If you carry on with that acceptance of
it's London and it's part of the scene,

00:16:18.964 --> 00:16:20.125
I'm just going to do it,

00:16:20.425 --> 00:16:27.110
that process of engaging may increase and
then you will

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:27.891
develop a habit.

00:16:29.352 --> 00:16:33.275
The idea of abstinence is that when you're
trying to rewrite neural pathways is the

00:16:33.276 --> 00:16:33.976
way to go.

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:38.362
You're giving yourself every opportunity
to create new experience and it's a new

00:16:38.422 --> 00:16:40.884
experience which challenges the
neuroplasticity

00:16:41.404 --> 00:16:43.485
which then creates the change in the
brain.

00:16:50.829 --> 00:16:54.771
The sheer quantity of treatments on offer
at Paracelsus can often feel like a way to

00:16:54.791 --> 00:16:55.912
justify the price tag.

00:16:57.693 --> 00:17:01.235
But the main focus is therapy and if it
eventually forced me to engage with my

00:17:01.275 --> 00:17:03.196
issues it can do the same for the 1%.

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:10.742
As much as we love to pile in on rich
people, I guess wealth can sometimes be a

00:17:10.762 --> 00:17:12.643
gilded cage that leads to isolation.

00:17:14.244 --> 00:17:17.706
But for those of us who can't hire a team
of people to make us feel better whenever

00:17:17.746 --> 00:17:21.208
we want, a church hall and a few chairs

00:17:21.268 --> 00:17:22.008
are just as good.

00:17:23.229 --> 00:17:27.531
And there's probably a reason it's unusual
for therapists to sit with you for all

00:17:27.571 --> 00:17:29.993
your meals and refer to themselves as your

00:17:30.073 --> 00:17:30.893
symbolic dad.

00:17:32.914 --> 00:17:34.095
I'm excited to get back.

00:17:34.395 --> 00:17:35.876
I'm excited to have a glass of wine.

00:17:36.728 --> 00:17:37.870
I probably shouldn't say that.

